Subject: [PATCH] scrub: neutral placeholders for user-home and studio paths in
 the tracked text that remains

Tracked-file sweep, lines: user-home 220 -> 114 (36 -> 15 files); studio-path 2826 -> 1615 (235 -> 54 files); credential/token shapes 0 throughout. Three more internal run scripts the first scope pass missed (a hyphenated stem the pattern did not match) are removed: r53-route-probe.cmd, r58-build-server.cmd, r58-q6k-repeat.cmd.

TARGET 0 IS NOT REACHED AND THE REMAINDER IS NOT HIDDEN. 112 user-home and 1,597 studio-path lines live in patches/series/*.patch, which is GENERATED from git: editing those files in place breaks , whose whole claim is byte-identity to a fresh generation, and regenerating them means rewriting the source commits. Both costs are real; neither is paid here. This is the second thing the proposed export branch would fix.

Also left alone, deliberately: arifi_sync.py's STUDIO_ROOT and sources.json's turbomerge url are values read at RUN TIME, not prose - substituting a placeholder would make the code and the config describe a path that does not exist, which is a behaviour change dressed up as a scrub (SF-P4). docs/backend/snapdragon/windows.md is upstream content. The rig hostnames are the intentional disclosure and the qnap hits were reviewed and cleared as a base64 token and an integrity hash.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release engineering for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - text substitution in documents and one build-cache snapshot; no code path is touched.
